    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0889c295e74d46d186d273da42cd194e",
      "statement": "FeedPollingService.pollFeed looks up the feed outside its try/catch (so a missing feed throws NotFoundException that propagates to the caller), performs a conditional fetch with ETag/Last-Modified, short-circuits on 304 by only updating lastPolledAt, and otherwise parses the body and inserts only articles not already present for (feed_id, guid) via articleRepository.existsByFeedIdAndGuid.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/service/FeedPollingService.java#L31-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:78f5c36e2e8a630187d2bb7b66176f3313cd3a2ed9a4e279ee1cbfcf5cab3321:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ae5395dd6abb447694f5b42eedea66c8",
      "statement": "On a successful poll, FeedPollingService resets errorCount to 0, clears lastError, updates lastSuccessfulPollAt and lastPolledAt, and saves the feed before publishing ArticlesIngestedEvent for any newly inserted article ids; on any exception during fetch/parse/save, it increments errorCount, records lastError, updates lastPolledAt, saves the feed, and swallows the exception (logs only) so a bad poll never crashes the scheduler thread.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/service/FeedPollingService.java#L36-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39d61bc1445cd62b080b76c0ceaed4043d13efd3dcea685cc2aa7e74c129b077:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3e5abb6e09144bdc8dbdee24372a3a9d",
      "statement": "FeedPollingService publishes ArticlesIngestedEvent(feedId, newIds) only when newIds is non-empty, and wraps the publish in its own try/catch so a scoring-side RuntimeException cannot be misattributed to poll failure (errorCount bookkeeping happens before and independently of this publish).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/service/FeedPollingService.java#L75-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0330d61820aac0f5074c5ff9b80507074ee0913f1bd1ce0f6f65fa1e819321d3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d0d4d53481c443638d3340f7dcecbdb9",
      "statement": "FeedPollingScheduler.pollAndAdjust re-reads the feed's current error state from the database after each poll and recomputes the effective interval via computeEffectiveInterval: once errorCount >= backoffThreshold (default 5), the interval is pollIntervalMinutes * 2^(errorCount / backoffThreshold) using integer division and an exponent capped at 30, clamped to maxIntervalMinutes (default 1440); otherwise the interval is just pollIntervalMinutes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/MyfeederProperties.java#L45-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d9a27960e1c27b3cea37c0286636143ed7b0b7f9d97821997c42f6289ec4d0f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/scheduler/FeedPollingScheduler.java#L79-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20df92db0bc1122b868d22265b3cca6c41018f51b21c6c3dc0bd6e9f1a879d9a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e1f44c00f1534d02afd0270cc2f2d2a9",
      "statement": "When the recomputed effective interval differs from the currently scheduled one, FeedPollingScheduler cancels and replaces the scheduled task starting one full interval from now; this re-evaluation is itself wrapped in a try/catch that logs a warning and keeps the current schedule if it fails, so a transient DB error cannot silently unschedule a feed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/scheduler/FeedPollingScheduler.java#L86-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c4d20c46ce34236f39c77b49552d2c4a2cb04e0ae10b3ea28d3ab83fb3b1827:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d6c6de1a12374238becaa6cdc65487ad",
      "statement": "FeedPollingScheduler.pollAndAdjust cancels the feed's scheduled task if pollFeed throws NotFoundException, covering the case where the feed was deleted concurrently with a scheduled poll; a comment in the scheduler explicitly accepts a race between external registerFeed/cancelFeed calls and this self-replacement as acceptable for a single-user deployment.",
      "evidence": [
